# TypeScript Rules

## Core
- Strict mode is on — no workarounds
- Zero `any`. Use `unknown` and narrow it, or define a proper type
- No type assertions (`as SomeType`) unless you can justify it in a comment
- Prefer `interface` for object shapes; `type` for unions, intersections, and aliases

## Components & Functions
- All component props get an explicit interface: `interface CardProps { ... }`
- All functions have explicit return types — especially async functions and API helpers
- Use discriminated unions for components with meaningfully different states

## Patterns
- Use `unknown` for error catches: `catch (err: unknown)`
- Validate external data at the boundary (Strapi API responses) — don't trust and spread
- Avoid non-null assertion (`!`) — handle the null case explicitly

## Naming
- Boolean variables: `isLoading`, `hasError`, `canSubmit`
- Event handlers: `handleClick`, `handleSubmit`
- Directories: `kebab-case` — components use `PascalCase` filenames